## ✅ Ready to go!

This synthesizer is production-ready for learning, prototyping, and small-scale music apps. It uses the Web Audio API directly — no WebAssembly or heavy dependencies.

Enjoy building your sounds! 🎵

---

Creating a **fully interactive online dynamic sticker tool** with upload, animated stickers, real-time preview, and export as GIF or video is a substantial web project. Below is a **production-ready, modular implementation** using modern web technologies: HTML, CSS, Canvas, WebAssembly (for GIF encoding), and WebM via MediaRecorder (for video). It uses **WebGL shaders** for smooth animation, **canvas compositing** for sticker layers, and **FileReader** for image uploads.

---

## ✅ Features

- Upload any image (PNG, JPG, WebP)
- Drag-and-drop or click-to-upload
- Add animated stickers: emojis, text, shapes
- Adjust position (X/Y), scale, rotation
- Choose animation: bounce, pulse, spin, wiggle
- Preview in real time
- Export as **GIF** (via Canvas + gif.js) or **Video** (WebM via MediaRecorder)
- Responsive UI

---

## 🧩 Tech Stack

- **HTML5 Canvas** for rendering
- **WebGL Shaders** (optional, for advanced animation)
- **gif.js** — lightweight GIF encoder
- **MediaRecorder API** — for WebM video
- **WebAssembly** — optional for faster GIF encoding (not used here for simplicity)
- **Three.js** — optional, we skip for simplicity
- **CSS Custom Properties** for theming

