Creating a fully self-hosted, privacy-respecting, offline-capable screenshot tool is complex and typically requires headless browsers (like Puppeteer or Playwright) and server infrastructure. However, I can provide you with a **client-side demo** that uses the **HTML5 Canvas + screenshot capture API** (via `html2canvas` or `dom-to-image`) — which works in the browser without server dependencies, but **only captures the current tab or a visible DOM**, not arbitrary remote URLs.

> ⚠️ **Important Limitation**: Client-side tools **cannot** capture arbitrary remote URLs (e.g., `https://example.com`) without user interaction because of browser security restrictions (CORS, sandboxing). You must either:
> - Allow the user to navigate to the URL first, then capture (simplest),
> - Or host a proxy server (e.g., with Puppeteer/Playwright) to fetch and render the page.

