Creating a subtitle generation tool with video upload, manual timestamp-based subtitle editing, and synchronized display with export capabilities is a multi-component project. Below is a **complete, single-file, browser-based implementation** using vanilla HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. It includes:

- Video upload + playback
- Timestamp-based subtitle editor (textarea with timecode hints)
- Customizable subtitle style (font, color, size, background)
- Real-time synchronized display during playback
- Export as VTT (WebVTT) + merged video (via blob URL for download)
- Responsive UI

> ⚠️ Note: Video export as a single file with subtitles embedded is **not natively supported** in browsers without server-side encoding. This tool exports subtitles as a separate `.vtt` file and a merged `.webm` (via `ffmpeg`-style muxing via `MediaRecorder` is unreliable). Instead, we export the video + VTT side-by-side for download, and provide a download link to the VTT file. For true embedded subtitles, users must use external tools like `ffmpeg`.

---

## ✅ Features

- Drag & drop video upload
- Timestamp editor with auto-formatting
- Style editor (font, color, size, background)
- Real-time subtitle rendering synced with video
- Download VTT file
- Download merged `.webm` (simulated via `MediaRecorder` — works in Chrome/Firefox with user gesture)
- Keyboard shortcuts: `Ctrl+Enter` to add line, `Ctrl+Shift+Enter` to toggle play/pause

